# Security headers for hosting platforms that respect this file (Netlify,
# Cloudflare Pages). Other platforms need equivalent configuration.
#
# CSP is now shipped from this file. This SUPERSEDES the earlier deliberate
# decision to delegate it to the deployment platform.
#
#   Why that decision was made: the Supabase project URL is injected at build
#   time, so a static policy committed here could not name the actual project
#   and connect-src would either be wrong or wide open.
#
#   Why reversing it is safe now: `vite.config.ts` validates VITE_SUPABASE_URL
#   (parseable, https except for localhost/127.0.0.1) and substitutes the two
#   markers below during `closeBundle`, then asserts that no marker survives. A
#   misconfigured production build fails instead of emitting a policy with
#   literal placeholders, and no real project URL is ever committed here.
#
#   Still required from the operator: platforms that ignore `_headers` need the
#   equivalent configuration applied by hand.

/*
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; base-uri 'self'; object-src 'none'; frame-ancestors 'none'; form-action 'self'; script-src 'self'; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; img-src 'self' data: blob: __SUPABASE_HTTP_SRC__ https://images.unsplash.com; media-src 'self' data: blob: __SUPABASE_HTTP_SRC__; font-src 'self' data:; connect-src 'self' __SUPABASE_CONNECT_SRC__; worker-src 'self'; manifest-src 'self'
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(self), geolocation=(), payment=(), usb=()
  X-DNS-Prefetch-Control: off
